-- title:
--   Cyclic rotation and exchange Cayley graph
-- statement:
--   Let the states on $n$ positions be all permutations. Define forward rotation $L$ as the cyclic permutation and backward rotation $R$ as its inverse. For positive $n$, define $X$ as the transposition of cyclic positions zero and one, and form the simple multiplication Cayley graph generated by $L,R,X$. Words in three corresponding letters evaluate by multiplying their assigned permutations in list order, with the empty word evaluating to the identity. Positions zero and one may coincide in dimension one. The bundle also supplies left translation as a graph homomorphism for any multiplication Cayley graph of a group. These definitions fix the graph and word conventions.
